#: src/guida.c:85
msgctxt "guida"
msgid ""
"AMS lets administrators send text messages to the users of the machine and "
"know who has read them. Messages appear in terminals (console, ssh, desktop "
"terminals, tmux) and on the desktop, in a dialog with the buttons «I have "
"read it» and «Later»; whoever is not logged in finds them at the next login. "
"Every message asks for a read confirmation and AMS asks again until the user "
"gives it, without ever blocking their work. Each user sees AMS in their own "
"language. The command is reserved to administrators (sudo or wheel group) "
"and re-runs itself with sudo."
msgstr ""

